> _Build-mode memory: minimal. Most of what you need is in the code._

## Layer 1 — Session memory

In-flight conversation only. Nothing to persist across sessions for a normal CLI/library project.

## Layer 2 — Change log

Major design decisions you make in this project should be recorded as:

- A clear commit message ("Adopt `unittest` (not pytest) per maintainer's call in #12")
- A short note in `.harness/CHANGES.md` if you want it discoverable outside git log
- A doc update in `README.md` if user-facing

## Layer 3 — Dependency rationale

When you add a dep to `pyproject.toml`, also add a one-line note explaining *why* — either as a `# comment` above the line or in `CHANGES.md`. Future agents will not re-justify a dep that's already there but they will remove ones they can't justify.

